{"content":[{"c":["ZATTU"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Clan chief with whom 945 people returned with Zerubbabel (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.8","r":"Ezra.2.8","rawR":"Ezra.2.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.8","value":"Ezra.2.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.13","r":"Neh.7.13","rawR":"Neh.7.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.13","value":"Neh.7.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:13"}," cites 845 returnees). Of the priests who renounced their foreign wives, six are listed as “sons” of Zattu (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.27","r":"Ezra.10.27","rawR":"Ezra.10.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.27","value":"Ezra.10.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:27"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. One of the chiefs of the people who signed Nehemiah’s covenant (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.14","r":"Neh.10.14","rawR":"Neh.10.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.14","value":"Neh.10.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 10:14"},"); perhaps the same person as #1 above."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Zattu","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ezr 2:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.2.8","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.2.8","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.2.8"},{"anchorText":"Neh 7:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.7.13","rawQueryValue":"Neh.7.13","sourceRefExact":"Neh.7.13"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 10:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.27","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.27","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.10.27"},{"anchorText":"Neh 10:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.10.14","rawQueryValue":"Neh.10.14","sourceRefExact":"Neh.10.14"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"63e6b2b071ab184547e84ca0ed24091178b515320ef61595cfab40bcdb2dd3d9","sourceItemName":"Zattu